@startuml
/' docs/sds/diagrams/export-pipeline.puml — one content model, three SKUs, refusals before bytes.
   Implements: SDS §11. Register: C-5 (projection union), C-15 (exporter class), C-22
   (enumerated snapshot, pinned clock, refusal), O-18/O-19 (VACUUM INTO + quiescence counts),
   O-24 (lockfile + CI build), O-20 (PII classes). '/
title Export pipeline — three SKUs from one content model

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam activityBorderColor #555555
skinparam activityBackgroundColor #FDFDFD

start

:operator: export <tenant> --target cms|astro|static;

:open an **exporter** connection\n(short-lived, never pooled, never in a transaction);
note right
  The only class permitted to run VACUUM INTO (C-15).
  The render class is query_only=1 and cannot.
end note

:wal_checkpoint(TRUNCATE);
:quiescence: count every exported table\nsource-before, source-after, snapshot-in;
if (all three agree within 5 attempts?) then (yes)
else (no)
  :refuse SKW_E_EXP_NOT_QUIESCENT;
  stop
endif
note right
  O-19: a cp-built bundle with a manifest measured from
  the copy passes 27/27 checks and serves 201 of 241
  pages. Counts are the gate; a manifest is not.
end note

:VACUUM INTO data/site.db   (the only correct copy);
:apply the projection union;
note right
  set(tables in sqlite_master) ==
  core (schema/export-projection.json)
  + u_* (prefix rule: rows)
  + p_<id>_* (installed manifest tables[].export)
  Anything left over is a build failure (C-5).
  modes: rows | empty | filtered
end note

:classify every file\ncontent | media | pii | secret | db | infra;
:pin the clock: SKW_EXPORT_NOW;

if (target == cms) then (yes)
  :preflight: gated assets present?;
  if (gated assets?) then (yes)
    :refuse SKW_E_EXP_GATED_ASSETS (named keys);
    stop
  endif
  :write compose (4 services, pinned digests)\n.env (generated secrets, never populated in the bundle)\ndata/control.seed.json (1 tenant, mode=production,\n  1 owner with must_change=1)\ncontent/ · data/site.db · install.sh;
elseif (target == astro) then (yes)
  :preflight: gated assets? forms without an action URL?\nparameterised sources with a `free` param in a link?;
  if (any refusal?) then (yes)
    :refuse: SKW_E_EXP_GATED_ASSETS |\nSKW_E_PL_EXPORT_FORWARD_NO_TARGET |\nSKW_E_EXP_PARAMETERISED;
    stop
  endif
  :enumerate each source's declared parameter domains\n(cross product <= SKW_SNAPSHOT_MAX_COMBOS = 1024,\n <= 2 MB per source);
  :generate src/pages/*.astro + src/content/*.json snapshots\n+ package.json + the package-lock.json it resolved\n+ README with the exact deploy commands;
  :CI runs npm ci && npm run build on the generated target\nand records the build id in BUNDLE.json;
else (static)
  :same preflight, and the same enumeration;
  :render one .html per (path, parameter combination)\n+ assets/ + robots.txt + sitemap.xml;
  :two exports of one DB at one SKW_EXPORT_NOW are byte-identical\n(asserted on the projection digest, check 16);
endif

:exclude, in every target:
content/protected/wm/**  (per-buyer renders, class pii)
content/sources/**       (never shipped)
data/control.db, any -wal or -shm, a populated .env;
note right
  O-08 measured a naive bundle at 8,739,862 B and the
  sealed one at 224,983 B on the same fixture. Both
  numbers come from the same run.
end note

:write BUNDLE.json (schema skunkworks/site-bundle/v3)\ncreated_at · export_now · tenant{key,mode,db_version}\nhosts · image{app_digest,runner_digest} · projection_version\nsource_counts · files[] with sha256+class · plugins[]\nrefusals[] · notes[];
:generate EXPORT-NOTES.md from notes[];
:ship cold: journal_mode=delete (what VACUUM INTO produces);

:install.sh --verify  (pinned image, bundle mounted :ro);
if (BUNDLE.json present, every sha256 matches,\nno -wal in the tree, source_counts match?) then (yes)
  :exit 0;
else (no)
  :exit 12;
  stop
endif

stop

@enduml
